{title: Harbour Lights}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}
{tempo: 92}
{subtitle: Sung in %{key}%{tempo| at %{} bpm}}
# Exercises ChordPro 6: grid, annotations, selectors, %{} substitution,
# delegated notation, a text block and a second song in one file.
{comment-guitar: Capo off, let it ring}
{comment-ukulele: Ukulele: play it up the neck}

{start_of_grid label="Intro" shape="1+4x2+1"}
Intro || G . . . | C~D . . . | Em . . . | D . . . |
      |  G . . . | C . D .   | G . . . | G . . . || x2
{end_of_grid}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Lamps along the [C]harbour wall, [*rit.][D]slowly
[Em]Nets are drying, [C]gulls call [D]low
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Bring the boats home, [C]bring them [G]in
[C]Light the lights for [D]all our [G]kin
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_abc}
X:1
K:G
GABc d2 d2|
{end_of_abc}

{start_of_textblock label="Note"}
Hum the last line once more, then stop.
{end_of_textblock}

{new_song}
{title: Harbour Lights (reprise)}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse}
[G]Lamps along the [C]harbour [D]wall [*hold]
[Em]All the boats are [D]home at [G]last
{end_of_verse}
